seg-0c26ec09bf16 = SISRE is the message's representation error against the truth it was fitted to; orbit determination and orbit prediction error are not modelled. (result <c1/>)

# text
# c1: limitations[1]
seg-3762de39de07 = The truth orbit is a Kshana numerical integration (zonal or EGM2008 gravity, static exponential drag), not a real satellite's precise orbit; no third body, solar radiation pressure or tides. (result <c1/>)

# text
# c1: limitations[2]
seg-4486dd350b57 = The binary format is Kshana's own documented encoding modelled on the published message components; it is not the bit layout of Celeste or any other system (none is public). (result <c1/>)

# text
# c1: limitations[3]
seg-2a5c1bce8320 = The RINEX-style block is a documented Kshana extension; RINEX { "4.02" } defines no LEO navigation records. (result <c1/>)

# text
# c1: limitations[4]
seg-642d8f4d60e7 = NeQuick-G coefficients are carried and the effective ionisation level is computed, but the NeQuick electron-density integration that turns it into a delay is not implemented; the Klobuchar delay is, scaled to the carrier by 1/f^{ "2" } with no correction for a satellite flying inside the ionosphere. (result <c1/>)

# text
